{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAQfM7qqfTYVVF5ETsHY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I changed `Hijack` in `response_writer.go` so it fails only once body bytes have been written (`w.size > 0`). Before, it also failed when only the headers had been sent (for example after `WriteHeaderNow()`), which breaks WebSocket libraries that send the 101 status first and then hijack the connection.\n\nI added a test case to `TestResponseWriterHijackAfterWrite` for hijacking after only the headers are written. GATE PASS: the hijack tests fail without the source change and pass with it. Format and leftover-debug checks are clean.\n\nHijacking after a body write is still rejected, as before. I only ran the hijack tests, not the full suite, and I didn't try it with a real WebSocket library."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1330,"cache_read_input_tokens":33733,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1330,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":237,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7fc7abbf-61ec-49fb-902b-d77d7e544a44","uuid":"73d367b0-66cb-4087-b3ea-1336e80ce458","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:25:34.675Z","request_id":"req_011CgAQfLrU9g4A3Q1FXACdN"}
